h1. User Story

*As an* admin
*I want to* use CMS to upload and manage banners for Platinum Business Hub Homepage
*So that I* can display promotional and informational banners to visitors on the homepage

h1. Background

The CMS currently has banner functionality that needs to be adjusted/configured specifically for the Platinum Business Hub Homepage. Admins should be able to upload, manage, and display banners through the existing CMS interface at https://ide.ioh.co.id/cms/login.

----

h1. Acceptance Criteria

h2. AC1: Banner Upload and Management Interface

*Given* I am logged into the CMS as an admin
*When* I navigate to the banner management section
*Then* I should see:
* A dedicated section or category for "Platinum Business Hub Homepage" banners
* Options to upload new banners
* A list of existing banners with their status (active/inactive)
* Edit and delete controls for each banner
* Preview capability before publishing

h2. AC2: Banner Upload Specifications

*Given* I am uploading a banner for Platinum Business Hub Homepage
*When* I select an image file
*Then* the system should:
* Accept common image formats (JPG, PNG, WebP, GIF)
* Validate image dimensions (recommended: minimum 1920x600px for desktop)
* Validate file size (maximum 2MB per banner)
* Show preview of uploaded image
* Allow me to set banner display order/priority
* Allow me to set active/inactive status
* Allow me to set start and end dates for banner display (optional)
* Allow me to add alt text for accessibility
* Allow me to set click-through URL (optional)

h2. AC3: Banner Display on Homepage

*Given* there are active banners configured for Platinum Business Hub Homepage
*When* a user visits the Platinum Business Hub Homepage
*Then*:
* The banner should be displayed in the designated banner area (upper right based on existing description)
* If multiple active banners exist, they should rotate/carousel automatically
* The banner should be responsive and display correctly on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices
* The banner image should load with proper lazy loading for performance
* If a click-through URL is configured, clicking the banner should navigate to that URL
* The banner should respect the active date range if configured

h2. AC4: Multiple Banner Support with Carousel

*Given* multiple banners are active for the same date/time
*When* the homepage loads
*Then*:
* Banners should display in a carousel/slider format
* Auto-rotation should occur every 5 seconds (configurable)
* User should see navigation dots/indicators showing total banners and current position
* User should be able to manually navigate between banners using previous/next controls
* Carousel should pause on hover (desktop) or touch interaction (mobile)

h2. AC5: Banner Performance and Optimization

*Given* banners are configured
*When* the homepage loads
*Then*:
* Banner images should be optimized and cached
* Page load time should not exceed 3 seconds with banner loading
* Images should be served via CDN if available
* Lazy loading should be implemented for below-the-fold banners

h2. AC6: Mobile Responsiveness

*Given* a user accesses the homepage from a mobile device
*When* the page loads
*Then*:
* Banner should resize appropriately for mobile screens
* Alternative mobile-specific banner images can be uploaded (optional)
* Touch gestures (swipe) should work for banner navigation
* Banner should not break page layout on any device size

----

h1. Business Rules and Constraints

* At least one active banner must be configured for the homepage to display the banner section
* If no active banners exist, the banner area should be hidden gracefully
* Banner display order should follow priority number (1 = highest priority)
* Expired banners should automatically stop displaying
* Maximum 10 active banners at any given time to prevent performance issues
* Only admins with CMS access can upload and manage banners
* Banners must comply with brand guidelines (this should be documented separately)

h1. Error Handling and Edge Cases

*File Upload Errors:*
* If file format is invalid → Show error: "Please upload a valid image file (JPG, PNG, WebP, GIF)"
* If file size exceeds limit → Show error: "File size must be less than 2MB. Please compress your image."
* If dimensions are too small → Show warning: "Image dimensions are below recommended size. Banner may appear pixelated."
* If upload fails → Show error: "Upload failed. Please try again or contact support."

*Display Errors:*
* If banner image fails to load on homepage → Display placeholder or hide banner gracefully
* If no active banners → Hide banner section entirely (no empty space)
* If API call fails → Use cached banners if available, or hide section

*Edge Cases:*
* Concurrent banner edits by multiple admins → Last save wins, with timestamp tracking
* Banner scheduled for future date → Should not display until start date/time
* Banner with past end date → Should stop displaying immediately

h1. UX/UI Considerations

* Banner carousel should have smooth transitions (fade or slide)
* Loading state should show skeleton/shimmer while banner loads
* Accessibility: All banners must have alt text for screen readers
* Accessibility: Carousel controls must be keyboard navigable
* Admin interface should show thumbnail previews for easy identification
* Admin interface should show banner status with clear visual indicators (green = active, gray = inactive, yellow = scheduled)

